   326	
   327	## 9. Risks the review should attack
   328	
   329	1. The projection doubles write volume on both engines. QLever's O(delta) update cost may make the
   330	   current graph too expensive to maintain at 256 clients with steady writes.
   331	2. H-X-CUT may fail on an edge (aborted transactions, restarts, compaction), leaving recorded-time
   332	   reads on the slow ledger.
   333	3. Index tables in XTDB turn every write into several documents in the single writer, which may cap
   334	   write throughput below the load target.
   335	4. The KV oracle shares Triplex core code with the system under test, so a core bug can pass the
   336	   entity suite on both sides.
   337	5. The 60 GiB VM disk and 12 GiB RAM may not hold the 10m-entity rung for either engine.
   338	6. Scope: 57 XTQL task ports, two projections, two write protocols, two scale ladders and a load
   339	   harness is a lot of work; the loop may spread thin across tracks.
   340	
   341	## 10. Resume protocol
   342	
   343	`lab/STATE.md` is updated at every dispatch and every completion with running agents, branches and
   344	slots, pending decisions and the next three actions. After any context compaction the orchestrator
   345	reads `lab/STATE.md`, `lab/SCORECARD.md` and the notebook tail before acting.
